{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev","id":316262,"title":"The Freaks Come Out At Night: Centimani ( Open Dev )","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-19T07:42:56-08:00","id":316262,"title":"The Freaks Come Out At Night: Centimani ( Open Dev )","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-promethean-the-created/\" target=\"_blank\">The Freaks are all over the town... </a><br /> <br /> (Comment Repost)<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like implications of transhumanism thinking for Prometheans to gone in the murderous rampage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One progresses on the Pilgrimage, or one degrades. No progress toward the New Dawn is possible while a Promethean follows the Refinement of Flux. </div> </div> </div>So there is no way of saying \u201cI abstain from Pilgrimage, but not want to dwell in to Flux\u201d?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T08:15:21-08:00","id":316294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev#post316262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there is no way of saying \u201cI abstain from Pilgrimage, but not want to dwell in to Flux\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>One stalls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T08:36:49-08:00","id":316316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev#post316262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there is no way of saying \u201cI abstain from Pilgrimage, but not want to dwell in to Flux\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like it\u2019s a bad thing. <br /> <br /> That said, take another look at Stannum. A case <i>could</i> be made (and <i>was</i> made, in <b>Strange Alchemies</b>) that Stannum can serve as a sort of \u201cholding pattern\u201d for the Pilgrimage. In fact the \u201cBasic Refinements\u201d spoiler pointed out that Stannum serves as a \u201csafety net\u201d of sorts, giving you a way to abandon your current Refinement without being forced to join the Centimani. Unless, of course, Stannum <i>is</i> your current Refinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:19:10-08:00","id":316342,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Stannum as a holding point makes a lot more sense - thematically and philosophically - than the Refinement of Flux.<br /> Look at Vengeance (capital V) in literature and myth; look at Fury, Wrath. From &quot;The Illiad&quot; to &quot;Othello&quot; and &quot;Macbeth&quot; all the way up through &quot;Kill Bill.&quot; There's some pathos, there, and it's pretty easy to understand even from today's cultural standpoint, but - do you *want* to be those people?<br /> At least you can identify them as people.<br /> <br /> The Centimanus are most decidedly not people, and at least you can recognize what kind of &quot;human&quot; experiences the Fury has had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:34:15-08:00","id":316347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev#post316262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t like implications of transhumanism thinking for Prometheans to gone in the murderous rampage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So there is no way of saying \u201cI abstain from Pilgrimage, but not want to dwell in to Flux\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Promethean</b> is not a transhumanist game. Don't expect it to be. <br /> <br /> To the second point, if you're abstaining from the Pilgrimage, you can kind of do that in any Refinement. You find a Role you like, and you sit there. You don't even generate Disquiet, if you do it right. <br /> <br /> Of course, there are consequences for your petulance/laziness/cowardice, which we'll cover when we get to Roles. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:45:00-08:00","id":316368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316347#post316347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Promethean</b> is not a transhumanist game. Don't expect it to be.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, there's something amusingly fitting about the Centimani being transhumanist characters. Transhumanism, at its core, is about rejecting humanity. So <i>of</i> <i>course</i> the result will be a horrifying monster with thoughts alien to our own. It's rejected everything that can bridge that gap of understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:52:53-08:00","id":316378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316347#post316347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Promethean</b> is not a transhumanist game. Don't expect it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is large gap between &quot;being transhumanist game&quot; and &quot;not punish the attitude of the transhumanists&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm just s bit off as write-up implay that doing transhumanism for your Created must lead you to Centimani madness.<br /> <br /> As to this...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316347#post316347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the second point, if you're abstaining from the Pilgrimage, you can kind of do that in any Refinement. You find a Role you like, and you sit there. You don't even generate Disquiet, if you do it right.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are consequences for your petulance/laziness/cowardice, which we'll cover when we get to Roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and Stannum -<br /> <br /> I think that best for &quot;I want to be a perfect being&quot; ( most transhuman stance ) would be be still a Ferrum thing - ones that still hold to long in it, forsaking goal of Humanity for being most perfect as Created, but still &quot;Azoth-ic&quot;. So for transhumanistic character pattern would be Ferrum-Stannum-Ferrum-Stannum-etc. Probably a bit boring, but it has some logic to it - you are overthrowing Humanity as a end goal, but still don't want to become mad Centimani. You get angry by the Azothic Memory it throws you on Golden Dawn road, when you want to stay what you are, maybe a bit more &quot;perfect&quot; - so here Stannum goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316368#post316368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, there's something amusingly fitting about the Centimani being transhumanist characters. Transhumanism, at its core, is about rejecting humanity. So <i>of</i> <i>course</i> the result will be a horrifying monster with thoughts alien to our own. It's rejected everything that can bridge that gap of understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you omit last &quot;<b>PtC</b> vs transhumanism&quot; discussion but those of fan ( like me ) that want a bit transhumanity leeway don't want to connect it with rampaging serial killers. We think that that best &quot;Created as transhumanist&quot; would be RoboCop - after failing few times in attaining Humanity he understands that he is needed as half-metal superbeing ( cop ) for the world. Nobel goal - becoming the best sword of justice, not &quot;I'm ssoooo special, I will kill everyone&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-19-2014, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:56:09-08:00","id":316380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316378#post316378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is large gap between &quot;being transhumanist game&quot; and &quot;not punish the attitude of the transhumanists&quot;.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but it's more &quot;the game doesn't care about transhumanist attitudes.&quot; I mean, <b>Promethean</b> is explicitly humanist. The whole point of the game is that these characters are striving for humanity, which is, in the context of the game, a desirable state. We're not going to put little disclaimers everywhere saying, &quot;Look, we know some folks like 'trans'humanism, where they want to be better than human, so if you want to do that, here's how.&quot; That's a different take on the game, and, as always, I'm fine with however you want to play it, but I'm keeping the game focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T11:11:32-08:00","id":316408,"title":"","content":"May I take a second to say that this has been said <i>many times</i>.<br /> <br /> To everyone who still feels like saying something about it, please internalize it and either accept it or the fact that you'll just have to house rule a lot when you get the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T11:46:05-08:00","id":316423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316378#post316378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get angry by the Azothic Memory it throws you on Golden Dawn road, when you want to stay what you are, maybe a bit more &quot;perfect&quot; - so here Stannum goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations. You've managed to go from missing the point to missing the point <i>super hardcore.</i><br /> <br /> Even in 1e, not every Promethean on the Pilgrimage was super driven to become human, but <i>no Promethean is satisfied with what they are.</i> Matt brought up dysphoria as a comparison in his interview on The Gentleman Gamer's podcast (and this jives with the sense I got rereading the line back in August that the Great Work is largely a pursuit to feel comfortable in your own skin by <i>making</i> it <i>your own</i> skin), and the Being-Created-As-Depression-Metaphor glasses I generally keep close to hand means I have no trouble understanding the borderline-if-not-outright-textual nature of being Hundred-Handed as comfortable misery.<br /> <br /> The character arc Stannum sets up as a philosophy is &quot;court Hope's two beautiful daughters so that you may Get Shit Done and learn about yourself as you scourge your idea of injustice and gradually develop a sense of proportionate response, patience, forgiveness, and the ability to let go, and then move on to another Refinement.&quot; It is not &quot;fuck the world i am a robot.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can theoretically &quot;stall&quot; forever on Ferrum with the excuse of getting everything &quot;perfect&quot; before you actually reach for the Aurora. You can do the same by hopping around the Refinements like a goddamn chimpanzee. The point of the exercise is that you not stifle, stunt, or stagnate in your endeavors, because that's the point where you've started to fucking <i>rot.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T11:51:09-08:00","id":316427,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling it'll get repeated quite a few times before all is said and done.<br /> <br /> Can I once again say that I appreciate that it seems like all dot ranking supernatural powers that aren't splat based are being put under the umbrella of Dread Powers? Just collecting them like that is a real nice, simple way to do it. Props to putting that in for Pandorans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T11:59:28-08:00","id":316429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316423#post316423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character arc Stannum sets up as a philosophy is &quot;court Hope's two beautiful daughters so that you may Get Shit Done and learn about yourself as you scourge your idea of injustice and gradually develop a sense of proportionate response, patience, forgiveness, and the ability to let go, and then move on to another Refinement.&quot; It is not &quot;fuck the world i am a robot.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because this isn't actually common knowledge, the &quot;court Hope's two beautiful daughters&quot; is a reference to this line:<br /> <b>\u201cHope has two beautiful daughters; their names are Anger and Courage. Anger at the way things are, and Courage to see that they do not remain as they are.\u201d \u2013 Augustine of Hippo</b><br /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T12:01:34-08:00","id":316431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316378#post316378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is large gap between &quot;being transhumanist game&quot; and &quot;not punish the attitude of the transhumanists&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Striving to be human is the central theme of the game - of course striving to NOT be human is bad thing. This is a central premise the entire game is build on.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for other examples of how to stall on the pilgrimage - trying to find peace in the Promethean condition without going Centimani sounds exactly like something an Originist (Plumbum) might do... until some explosion of Disquiet and Wasteland fucks their quest over and forces them back on the Pilgrimage of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T12:03:51-08:00","id":316433,"title":"","content":"It's odd that given the Centimani symbol there's never been any link between them and being the &quot;refinement&quot; of sulfur. I mean why use that symbol if you're not evoking sulfur?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T12:07:47-08:00","id":316435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316431#post316431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for other examples of how to stall on the pilgrimage - trying to find peace in the Promethean condition without going Centimani sounds exactly like something an Originist (Plumbum) might do... until some explosion of Disquiet and Wasteland fucks their quest over and forces them back on the Pilgrimage of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then of course &quot;find peace with the Promethean condition&quot; is practically a capsule summary of some strains of Cuprum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T12:46:18-08:00","id":316448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316378#post316378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you omit last &quot;<b>PtC</b> vs transhumanism&quot; discussion but those of fan ( like me ) that want a bit transhumanity leeway don't want to connect it with rampaging serial killers. We think that that best &quot;Created as transhumanist&quot; would be RoboCop - after failing few times in attaining Humanity he understands that he is needed as half-metal superbeing ( cop ) for the world. Nobel goal - becoming the best sword of justice, not &quot;I'm ssoooo special, I will kill everyone&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>....no.<br /> <a href=\"http://thepunchlineismachismo.com/archives/comic/im-not-sure-cyborgs-are-supposed-to-be-drinking-beer\" target=\"_blank\">I do not want to be Robocop. No one should want to be Robocop.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T14:43:06-08:00","id":316540,"title":"","content":"Fans of Promethean who want transhumanism in their Promethean aren't really fans of Promethean.<br /> <br /> It's a &quot;you're missing the entire point of the game&quot; kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 11-19-2014, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T14:52:41-08:00","id":316546,"title":"","content":"<br /> EDIT: Sorry about this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":2589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","user":"Magnum Opus","date":". 11-19-2014, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:02:21-08:00","id":316549,"title":"","content":"Guys, we don't need to knock on transhumanism to make it clear that Promethean is a humanist game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T15:21:17-08:00","id":316560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316448#post316448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://thepunchlineismachismo.com/archives/comic/im-not-sure-cyborgs-are-supposed-to-be-drinking-beer\" target=\"_blank\">I do not want to be Robocop. No one should want to be Robocop.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! That may be the beginning of the Promethean version of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xe1a1wHxTyo\" target=\"_blank\">Four Yorkshiremen</a>. <hr /><br /> I'm pretty ambivalent on this post.<br /> <br /> On the one hand I think the effects of Flux on the Promethean are very interesting. Their minds falling into Flux is great, and makes for good parallels with the Pandorans they seem to have command over. Flux is really just there for the true nadir of a Pilgrimage when Elpis is all but extinguished.<br /> <br /> What I don't like, though, is the black and white morality presented. No Centimanus can do good. No Lillithim can do good. The Pilgrimage is inherently good, and most of the reasons why one would fall to Flux could be otherwise expressed in one of the other Refinements.<br /> <br /> Humanity is chock full of utter bastards, and learning to be an utter bastard is just as valid a way to study humanity (as evidenced by Cobalus). Doing something disgustingly evil might be an essential Milestone on a Pilgrimage, or might even help attain the New Dawn. The fact that that Redeemed might just be irredeemable themselves doesn't make them less human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T16:29:27-08:00","id":316627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316560#post316560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't like, though, is the black and white morality presented. No Centimanus can do good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacrificing oneself to save one's throng from Pandorans would seem to put the lie to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No Lillithim can do good. </div> </div> </div>The Lilithim are monsters serving a Principle whose plans and desires you are not privy to and thus are inadvisable to emulate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Pilgrimage is inherently good, and most of the reasons why one would fall to Flux could be otherwise expressed in one of the other Refinements. </div> </div> </div>The Pilgrimage ultimately ends, one way or another, in the cessation of a potentially nightmarish Pyros-based strain on the world, and there are a plethora of ways to turn into a nihlistic serial killer without deciding coherent thought is overrated if it means you can't have a tentacle beard. Was there a point here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity is chock full of utter bastards, and learning to be an utter bastard is just as valid a way to study humanity (as evidenced by Cobalus). Doing something disgustingly evil might be an essential Milestone on a Pilgrimage, or might even help attain the New Dawn. The fact that that Redeemed might just be irredeemable themselves doesn't make them less human. </div> </div> </div>Humanist game. &quot;But what if assholes&quot; is a shit response in that it gleefully kickflips past the themes and necessary buy-in and you're beginning to tax my already-not-stellar reserves of patience by doing this. The game is going to be written to support the narratives it's being designed to work for. If you have a problem with this, you are welcome to change that in your own iteration of the material or opt out altogether, but complaining about the game doing as it's supposed to do in the base material is in poor taste and of extremely low worth this many repetitions in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-19-2014, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T18:09:52-08:00","id":316782,"title":"","content":"On the \u201cLilithim can do no good\u201d point, there\u2019s a sample Lilithim in <b>Pandora\u2019s Book</b> who puts the lie to this, by freeing a Promethean from a bunch of sadists and then proceeding to infect them with a horrible, disfiguring disease. Lilithm are destructive, not evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T21:04:57-08:00","id":316906,"title":"","content":"The Centimani are hands down my favorite &quot;protagonists antagonists&quot; in the NWoD.<br /> <br /> Their write up in the 1E book was excellent and only got better with their chapter in Pandora's Book that made them a very nuanced group akin to any other refinement in philosophy if not legitimacy. <br /> <br /> From this weeks blog I took away that it looks like a lot of the good from the Centimani in 1E is being retained, which is good. I was afraid that with Cobalt and Tin taking on some of the aspects of the more &quot;human aspect&quot; Centimani philosophy they wold look a little thin on the the ground. However, the inclusion of a more entropic self-breakdown (and the myriad reactions a person has to that) in their character type seems to &quot;bulk them out&quot; again be nicely. <br /> <br /> Not entirely sure at current that having them all be going mad one way or another and having problems with coherence of thought (I liked how frightening rational some of the 1E example Centimani were) is exactly my cup of tea, still I think it could be explored and implemented very well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316423#post316423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations. You've managed to go from missing the point to missing the point <i>super hardcore.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrdhamster missing the thematic and contextual point of a game? (Looks around) Hang on this is not a Demon thread! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry could not help myself. I'm obviously a bad person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T21:39:12-08:00","id":316935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316560#post316560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't like, though, is the black and white morality presented. No Centimanus can do good. No Lillithim can do good. The Pilgrimage is inherently good, and most of the reasons why one would fall to Flux could be otherwise expressed in one of the other Refinements.<br /> <br /> Humanity is chock full of utter bastards, and learning to be an utter bastard is just as valid a way to study humanity (as evidenced by Cobalus). Doing something disgustingly evil might be an essential Milestone on a Pilgrimage, or might even help attain the New Dawn. The fact that that Redeemed might just be irredeemable themselves doesn't make them less human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, and there are two Refinements that explicitly explore that point - Cobalus as you mentioned, and Stannum in its embrace of very human rage (all other Refinements are also capable of being villainous or doing immoral things to further their path, but those two are the most explicitly ABOUT that). The Centimani are something else entirely. They're &quot;evil&quot; from a humanist perspective because their nature makes them inimical to humanity, because they're the &quot;anti-humanity&quot; - they're not trans-humanity, they haven't transcended past it, they've gone in the complete opposite direction. The explorations of chaos, destruction, and mutation are inherently hostile to human life, as human life depends on reliable structured systems (social, biological, etc) to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T22:38:59-08:00","id":316958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316782#post316782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the \u201cLilithim can do no good\u201d point, there\u2019s a sample Lilithim in <b>Pandora\u2019s Book</b> who puts the lie to this, by freeing a Promethean from a bunch of sadists and then proceeding to infect them with a horrible, disfiguring disease. Lilithm are destructive, not evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite.<br /> <br /> I like to say that Lilithim are summoned when the Principle desires to break things. Some things really need to be broken.<br /> <br /> Honestly, this writeup makes one of my favored NPCs all the more viable; he's an Unfleshed, built as an autonomous defense system, who has given up on the idea he can be anything more. Thus the infinitely recursive path of Flux, as he neuters and harnesses monsters for the sake of whatever people he's currently protecting. <br /> <br /> I always meant him to be the Centimanus who can teach others about the Pilgrimage intentionally (it's not that he doesn't think it's a worthy goal, he just can't see himself completing it), and possibly saved from his own despair. With this, it's perfectly clear how self-defeating his pessimistic attitude actually is, and how he's ironically posing more of a danger rather than less like this (I previously had to rely on the irony of a place's defender creating a Wasteland as he really starts to settle in).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T02:02:22-08:00","id":317128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316906#post316906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrdhamster missing the thematic and contextual point of a game? (Looks around) Hang on this is not a Demon thread! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry could not help myself. I'm obviously a bad person.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably are. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's not that I don't get a point of the game - to become Human after Pilgrimage - only I have buddies that wants to play Promethean and ask &quot;Why would you always wanted to become Human?&quot;. And after answering them with &quot;because it's Noble Way for Created&quot; they still don't get it.<br /> <br /> Myself, a bit transhumanists, I'm a bit offended by the writing of Centimani from the post - connecting a supprasing the limits with serial killers. It's a bit like saying the prostetics limbs makes you kill people.<br /> <br /> But as <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">blackhatmatt </span></b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">stated - game is not written for people with a problems like mine - a bit pity, but I understand. Beside, they are some quasi-transhuman </span>Refinements - like Ferrum or Plumbum - they are very dark human - like Cobalus or Stannum. And there will be ways to stahl a Pilgrimage. For me as ST it's enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316935#post316935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because they're the &quot;anti-humanity&quot; - they're not trans-humanity, they haven't transcended past it, they've gone in the complete opposite direction. The explorations of chaos, destruction, and mutation are inherently hostile to human life, as human life depends on reliable structured systems (social, biological, etc) to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really support this view. Only I don't see this in the post. Maybe it wasn't stated enough that Centimani are reveling in the Chaos of the change, not amorality of it?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With that I end my transhumanity rant, because everyone will hang me on forum, even if <b>I'm</b> a fan of Promethean and really look for 2ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T03:10:43-08:00","id":317218,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm simplistic as hell, but I don't think you can transcend a thing you don't understand or are. So how can a Promethean be actually transhumanist by skipping completely the starting point, being human?<br /> <br /> If you want a transhumanist game of Promethean, make it so the objective of the characters once they achieved their New Dawns. Where do we go from here? if you must.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T03:51:35-08:00","id":317250,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> Still, you'd think by now people would twig that when the <i>Line Developer</i> said that part of the buy in is &quot;it's a humanist game&quot;, they stop expecting it to be anti-humanist/trans-humanist/post-humanist. And yes, that is the logical chain of reasoning. If you reject the humanist theme to the extreme, or try to stripe it out entirely from the story/system that was designed to encourge it, what you are left with is a broken mess.<br /> <br /> Even if the New Dawn is impossible at your table, it still needs to exist as an idea there for Promethean to work. An impossible dream has a powerful quality, especially as a motivation. As does the drive to fit in, be accepted or find your place in the world. Which is why the combination; which is built into their design (ie. they don't work without and were never meant too); is so compelling.<br /> <br /> Transhumanism is a different animal. Depending on your outlook, it can either be freeing (&quot;we can be so much more), or terrifying (&quot;You will be Upgraded&quot;). Either to takes the best of us and improves it, or takes the bad and makes it worse. But the good parts? They clash with humanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T04:37:34-08:00","id":317283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317218#post317218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm simplistic as hell, but I don't think you can transcend a thing you don't understand or are. So how can a Promethean be actually transhumanist by skipping completely the starting point, being human?</div> </div> </div> </div>With taking the Promethean state as it is, only fighting with drawbacks of it. Character like those I have in mind would question: &quot;Why Created need to be drawn by Disquiet? Why we are plagued by Torment? How can we suppress our Disfigurements?&quot;<br /> <br /> Character like that don't want to end the existence as Prometheans, cause they see they are superior to humanity in some ways - they can burn the Pyros, suppress human limitations, live longer. Really, without all the drawbacks of Created condition I totally see a valid idea of character that don't want to end it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317218#post317218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a transhumanist game of Promethean, make it so the objective of the characters once they achieved their New Dawns. Where do we go from here? if you must.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is with your definition of transhumanism - they don't need to be human to be <b>past</b> being human. For example, one of pillars of transhumanity is that you can <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uplift_(science_fiction)\" target=\"_blank\">Uplift</a> animals - dolphins don't need to be humans if they could be sapient and superinteligent in first place. Still, they will be &quot;persons&quot;, and have identities - and so they will be <b>trans</b>humans.<br /> <br /> So this characters would not see the need for ending the Pilgrimage, to become human. Because they don't want to be human in the first place. Or they would need another ending of it.<br /> <br /> For now, those type character is valid in mine as &quot;they are bit tragic, as Azothic Memory <b>wants</b> them human&quot;. Or even they can't fulfill they dreams because Principle have plan that is clashing with them. We talk about World of Darkness here - sometimes generally good thing ( idea of becoming human ) is bad for the PC, especially as enforced on him by outside source. And I will still support view that wanting to become something more than the Prometheans condition in the now state is still alchemy - you become something greater in alchemical process, only result is not the one that your colleges want.<br /> <br /> And still I wouldn't equate this with Centimani practices. Freaks want to ruin all the rules, not work <b>in side them</b>. They want total Flux transformation, were &quot;transhuman Prometheans&quot; would strive to they goal just by Azoth means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-20-2014, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T05:34:47-08:00","id":317312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317283#post317283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Really, without all the drawbacks of Created condition I totally see a valid idea of character that don't want to end it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot adequately express how completely and utterly missing the point of Promethean this statement is.<br /> <br /> Prometheans out of all the splats for the WoD never get to negate their weaknesses and flaws fully. Reality rejects them, they are sad, incomplete being that feel &quot;other&quot; in their own skin and desperately search for a way to &quot;belong&quot; to our world. One of the main points of the game is that all the &quot;cool stuff&quot; Prometheans get (that you mentioned Wyrd) are ultimately not as precious as humanity and belonging to a world that does not inherently reject you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317283#post317283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is with your definition of transhumanism - they don't need to be human to be <b>past</b> being human. For example, one of pillars of transhumanity is that you can <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uplift_(science_fiction)\" target=\"_blank\">Uplift</a> animals - dolphins don't need to be humans if they could be sapient and superinteligent in first place. Still, they will be &quot;persons&quot;, and have identities - and so they will be <b>trans</b>humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um...no. The idea of &quot;uplifting&quot; less developed species is a sci-fi trapping that ties into the idea of culture/technology progression an organisms development beyond its normal biological abilities (which is very similar to the transhuman ideal but not actually the same thing). Dolphins made super intelligent by cybernetics or gene-manipulation or whatever are &quot;transpersons/transdolphines&quot; not &quot;transhumans&quot;. Your mixing up the concept of &quot;person hood&quot; with humanity, the two are separate.<br /> <br /> So to provide the definition of transhumanism:<ul><li><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Noun</i> - the belief or theory that the <b>human race</b> can evolve beyond its current physical and mental limitations, especially <b>by means of science and technology</b>. </div> </div> </div></li> </ul>So, as mentioned here, for one to be transhuman, one would first need to be human. Something Prometheans are not.<br /> <br /> In addition, transhumanism engages with external forces to force an evolution e.g. advanced technology. Promethean is a game of internal &quot;alchemy&quot;. The characters progress towards humanity via their own experiences, conceptualizations and efforts. Azothic Memory gives them a direction to follow, but its not like its an active external force, its an internal drive they have (like birds have to migrate in the winter).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317283#post317283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For now, those type character is valid in mine as &quot;they are bit tragic, as Azothic Memory <b>wants</b> them human&quot;. Or even they can't fulfill they dreams because Principle have plan that is clashing with them. We talk about World of Darkness here - sometimes generally good thing ( idea of becoming human ) is bad for the PC, especially as enforced on him by outside source. And I will still support view that wanting to become something more than the Prometheans condition in the now state is still alchemy - you become something greater in alchemical process, only result is not the one that your colleges want.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm sure in your games you all transhuman Prometheans be a thing, please don't present it here as a thing the game SHOULD do or support.<br /> <br /> Why is the idea of becoming human, something that the Promethean feels an instinctual drive to pursue bad for the PC? How have they got it in their head that not being human is a better idea? Considering the major example they have of that is the Centimani? There is self delusion and rejection of the Pilgrimage of course, but then Flux embraces you and you join the Hundred Handed. Where in the setting does anything push them towards transhumanist thought and have that resonate as an idea that overcomes their drive to be human? Do they get some massive revelation from reading Julian Huxley or something?<br /> <br /> The Principle may or may not be directly influencing Prometheans. Azothic Memory is an internal drive, not an external force, so I don't see that as the Principle &quot;pulling the strings&quot; of Prometheans anymore then the God Machine is pulling the strings of the Unchained (see the parallel between Azothic Memory and the Cypher?). Quashimall do not appear to every Promethean, in fact they appear to relatively few if 1E is to be believed. I would say that those Prometheans that do get a divine visitation can be said to be influenced, I will agree to that much.<br /> <br /> Considering that a Promethean becoming human is equated with Lead becoming Gold, the pinnacle of Alchemy it would seem that a Promethean becoming something beyond human would involve an alchemical paradigm that would even be above that. Like making a nuclear bomb with no radioactive elements...which is to say, impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317128#post317128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really support this view. Only I don't see this in the post. Maybe it wasn't stated enough that Centimani are reveling in the Chaos of the change, not amorality of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Centimani = The &quot;Refinement&quot; of <b>Flux</b> (The clues in the title wyrdhamster, re-read Promethean E1 or Pandoras Book or both, both define/explain Flux and its connotations)<br /> <br /> Cliff notes version:<br /> <br /> Flux is inherently a chaotic, destructive and entropic force. Its the Divine Fire/Pyros &quot;negative&quot; aspect in contrast to Azoth. To follow Flux is to embrace a force that actively degrades and twists everything it touches.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are inherently creatures of Azoth, Flux's opposite, their Pilgrimage can only function if they cohere to a method of refining themselves. That's why Flux can't be the basis for a &quot;true&quot; refinement, as its impossible for it to &quot;refine&quot; anything, it inherently degrades, breaks down and destroys things.<br /> <br /> In alchemical terms Flux is complete dissolution without any possibility of distillation or coagulation back into a superior &quot;refined&quot; form.<br /> <br /> To come full circle back around to glamourweavers point: Flux is not &quot;trans&quot; anything, it can't move you &quot;beyond&quot; a point, it can only degrade you away from the point where you started. It is inherently anti-everything that needs coherence to function (such as biological life, human society, nuclear physics etc).<br /> <br /> Its not that the write up Matt posted &quot;did not support this&quot; (which is to say expressly state the nature of Flux) the simple truth that the Centimani follow Flux means this is a given fact about them (with individual variations obviously). One cannot grasp the full folly/tragedy of a Centimani without understanding the nature of Flux, the two are inseparable.<br /> <br /> If you really must look for transhumanist ideas in an innately humanist game (which we've already established is a <b>BAD IDEA</b>), the Centimani are not the place you should be looking basically. Though from your last post it seems you realize this now...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317218#post317218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm simplistic as hell, but I don't think you can transcend a thing you don't understand or are. So how can a Promethean be actually transhumanist by skipping completely the starting point, being human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, you can't have trans-human themes until you have humans in the picture as a baseline starting point.<br /> <br /> Prometheans have yet to even reach humanity, let alone any of the stuff that could come after. It would be very much a case of <b><i>&quot;trying to run before you have developed motor neurons&quot;</i></b>.<br /> <br /> I'm going to stop now, because this conversation is starting to look a lot like when I tried to explain the <b><i>&quot;Why?&quot;</i></b> of the aesthetics of Demon the Descent (namely the engagement with gnosticism, cyber-punk/post-cyber-punk divide, the espionage genre's tropes and how an optional side-bar in an optional splat-book should not dictate the direction of an entirely new gameline) to wyrdhamster and have him completely miss the point.<br /> <br /> Not to mention made me want to break things.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T06:54:34-08:00","id":317344,"title":"","content":"You could, I suppose, come up with a Refinement about mitigating the downsides of what you are now, without moving toward Elpis or Flux - and it would have to be a Refinement, because remaining the same takes effort when you're powered by the physical embodiment of change* - alchemically speaking, the Refinement of Salt would probably be the logical name. And give it Transmutations to suppress the way the Fire burns the world and people around it.<br /> <br /> * This probably being the source of the &quot;either progress or degrade&quot; comment.<br /> <br /> But it's not something the 2e, especially the core, particularly needs to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T09:57:06-08:00","id":317488,"title":"","content":"Cuprum or Plubbum, anyone?<br /> <br /> On a different note, if you really must talk about transhumanism in a humanist game, has anyone considered that Argentum can be interpreted as a being such as well as post-humanist? It's not a hardcore focus, since it's about humanity in the context of it's monsters, but some strains exist there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T11:38:54-08:00","id":317597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317488#post317488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cuprum or Plubbum, anyone?<br /> <br /> On a different note, if you really must talk about transhumanism in a humanist game, has anyone considered that Argentum can be interpreted as a being such as well as post-humanist? It's not a hardcore focus, since it's about humanity in the context of it's monsters, but some strains exist there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I've occasionally thought (though not out loud, because I don't want anyone to get the idea that I'm going to start including transhumanist themes in the game) that of all the Refinements, it's Argentum that comes the closest to &quot;wait, we can do better than human.&quot; <br /> <br /> But as I may have mentioned in the Complex Refinements post, other WoD creatures (the things that a Mystic studies) <i>aren't</i> &quot;better than human.&quot; They're in-human, or post-human, and they're all set apart from humanity in different ways. Part of being human is accepting the shit parts of being human, and that's part of the lesson of the Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> And, yeah, it's kind of antithetical to transhumanism. That isn't likely to change. But <b>Demon</b> is right over there! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T11:44:24-08:00","id":317601,"title":"","content":"Hell yeah Demon is right over there!<br /> <br /> But yeah, I wasn't crazy about touting Argentum as a possible transhumanist Refinment for those reasons. Still, I had to be fair-those chords are there and can be played, ideally with care and thought in regards to the humanism of the game.<br /> <br /> You know, a better train of thought is Athanors. Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-20-2014, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T12:55:06-08:00","id":317659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317597#post317597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, yeah, it's kind of antithetical to transhumanism. That isn't likely to change. But <b>Demon</b> is right over there! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Demon is a being that isn't human in the first place.<br /> <br /> Mage on the other hand...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T15:40:15-08:00","id":317732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317659#post317659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon is a being that isn't human in the first place.<br /> <br /> Mage on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... Portrays mages who attempt to transcend human mortality as one of its antagonist types?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T15:54:38-08:00","id":317743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317732#post317732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ... Portrays mages who attempt to transcend human mortality as one of its antagonist types?</div> </div> </div> </div>But also as one of its protagonist types, archmasters. Liches are bad news, forgoing Wisdom , stealing souls, and degrading themselves in a twisted understanding of their capabilities. Archmasters struggle with power, Wisdom, and purpose, and eventually come to the point where they move post the limitations of mortal flesh and soul and become gods. Seems a bit transhuman to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T18:41:06-08:00","id":317852,"title":"","content":"Being athletic, intelligent, attractive, and a slew of supernatural powers at the expense of social graces and social acceptance is a deal I feel like many 'gamers' (or anyone, really) like to think they would make. In reality, though? Probably not.<br /> <br /> You know what happens people with no fellow human contact or where everyone around them thinks they're a loser, or worse? <i>They lose their shit</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T19:59:48-08:00","id":317882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317743#post317743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But also as one of its protagonist types, archmasters. Liches are bad news, forgoing Wisdom , stealing souls, and degrading themselves in a twisted understanding of their capabilities. Archmasters struggle with power, Wisdom, and purpose, and eventually come to the point where they move post the limitations of mortal flesh and soul and become gods. Seems a bit transhuman to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the implication is that archmastery is an inherently unWise path, given Aponeia, and it's been spoilered that there are other paths to Ascenscion that do not involve the Golden Road. Then again, hubris is a coward's word and all that...<br /> <br /> Still, Mage is a better transhuman game. There are liches other than the Tremere, Morpheans (those who have possessed their own goetia and now exist in Astral Space as more-than-ghosts) and fully sapient ghost mages for one. Yes, I fully expect most liches are parasites or miserable (Morpheans have a hard time interacting with the waking world and learning new spells without stealing memories) but finding a path to non-malignant lichdom that gains more than it loses sounds like a worthy goal. Not to mention an archmaster can simply avoid causing Aponeia apart from their first; that definitely fits under positive transhumanism","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-20-2014, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T20:48:56-08:00","id":317901,"title":"","content":"Also, the <s>trans</s>post-humanist elements of the game aren\u2019t embedded in the archmasters, per se; they\u2019re embedded in Ascension, which can be achieved without becoming an archmaster. So archmasters are a bit of a red herring here; the core factor is that transcending human flesh and achieving true immortality is portrayed as a worthy goal \u2014 unless the Ascension appendix turns out very differently than I expect it to. <br /> <br /> That, and the fact that <b>Mage</b> portrays the bulk of humanity as being hobbled by a supernatural Curse that mages aren\u2019t subject to places mages firmly in transhuman territory; and Attainments push further in that direction. That the game emphasizes the dangers of attempting to transcend the human condition and the need to be very careful when doing so doesn\u2019t make it anti-transhumanist; it just emphasizes the (blatantly obvious IMHO) point that the path is a treacherous one, from which it is all to easy to detour. <br /> <br /> I could <i>definitely</i> see a Redeemed Promethean Awakening and deciding that the quest for Ascension is \u201cstage two of the Pilgrimage\u201d. If he Awakens as a Moros or otherwise attunes himself to Matter and its alchemical secrets (assuming that <b>Tome of the Mysteries</b>\u2019 Alchemy material is still a thing in 2e), such a conclusion is a very natural one to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T22:06:55-08:00","id":317946,"title":"","content":"As the writer of the Centimani section, I'd love to hear more feedback that isn't tied up in the whole transhumanism perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T22:24:00-08:00","id":317968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317946#post317946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the writer of the Centimani section, I'd love to hear more feedback that isn't tied up in the whole transhumanism perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much appreciation for providing a handy rationale for &quot;religious&quot; Centimani more evocative than &quot;a lot of them have tons of derangements&quot; and with more nuance than &quot;they're kooks.&quot;<br /> <br /> Likewise happy to see adherence to Flux put in terms like &quot;the grip of despair&quot; - stuff like that is good for getting across the essence of the Hundred-Handed as they came across in 1e with stuff like the Lady of Chains' pet conspiracy and the original writeup's sidebar about embracing dehumanization to try to avoid being hurt again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T00:59:13-08:00","id":318067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317901#post317901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and the fact that <b>Mage</b> portrays the bulk of humanity as being hobbled by a supernatural Curse that mages aren\u2019t subject to places mages firmly in transhuman territory; and Attainments push further in that direction. That the game emphasizes the dangers of attempting to transcend the human condition and the need to be very careful when doing so doesn\u2019t make it anti-transhumanist; it just emphasizes the (blatantly obvious IMHO) point that the path is a treacherous one, from which it is all to easy to detour.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mage is a horror game as well. It helps to underline how it's a few of the transhumanistic agendas that went horribly wrong before showing a few in which are going sort of right (Scions of God, Archmasters who simply wish to become one with the Arcana, etc). That and the characters are evolving from humanity proper into... Well, Gods if they reach that far.<br /> <br /> Of course, that has jack squat having to do with Promethean. While Mage has power unyielding, Promethean's power is namely exists as respites from the Alienation, Isolation, and Disquiet which allows the true miracles to happen. Person who chased you down before under the urging of disquiet now gives you an approving nod as you walk down the street. A hobby group that chased you out before now entertains you with their craft. A dog which yipped and shrieked at you now starts to accept you. A cruel existence briefly subsided to allow for chances at humanity. Herculean tasks that people take for granted every day.<br /> <br /> Hence why I keep picturing a Promethean coming up to a Mage working a spell while going on about transhumanism only to have said Promethean pick the Mage up by the neck and slapping him senseless while screaming and crying &quot;WHY DO YOU DO THIS!? YOU HAVE EVERYTHING I WANT AND NEED AND IT'S STILL NOT ENOUGH FOR YOU! WHAT KIND OF MONSTER ARE YOU!?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which then chokes the Mage resulting in the Promethean missing his milestone and having to continue his pilgrimage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T05:09:39-08:00","id":318170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317946#post317946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the writer of the Centimani section, I'd love to hear more feedback that isn't tied up in the whole transhumanism perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the sense of them being bound to chaos, and various ways they try to make what sense of that - and peace with it - they can. I like the sense of it as a philosophy that can become almost physical as it consumes you - like it's an anti-Vitriol and anti-Athanor as well as an anti-Refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T10:58:08-08:00","id":318359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317946#post317946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the writer of the Centimani section, I'd love to hear more feedback that isn't tied up in the whole transhumanism perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, thank you for attempting to get this treat back on track. And second, thank you for writing the Centimani section!<br /> <br /> Question: Are the Pandoran Dread Powers the same as the Pandoran Transmutations from First Edition? I'm less interested in the nuts-and-bolts than I am in the idea of there being any proper Centimani Transmutation(s) available in Second Edition. I always felt like the Freaks were scary for their powers, but they didn't really have much to suggest deeper exploration or meaning. I mean, a Pandoran who is appetite and change incarnate (even as <i>Sublimatus</i>) is a monster, but a thinking, scheming, 'I have a REASON' Centemanus is far worse than a monster... It becomes a terrible warning of what any of us could become. Giving the Centimani their own horrid Transmutations could go a long way towards them becoming antagonists that say, 'If only you knew the power of the Dark Side,&quot; a kind of villain-cum-monster.<br /> <br /> Also, might we see some terrible stigmata attached to the 'Refinement' of Flux? Not to bring up the term 'transhuman' again, but I think that Freaks ought to come with some nasty side effects that make them very clearly not-safe-for-player-character material. I dunno, like a Condition that cannot ever be removed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T11:40:01-08:00","id":318382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317946#post317946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the writer of the Centimani section, I'd love to hear more feedback that isn't tied up in the whole transhumanism perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a fair few other posters have already beat me to the key positive points I wanted to say you definitely covered even in the short write up that we got a preview of. I echo Phaolan's question about the potental for a &quot;Transmutation of Flux&quot;. Though I would also be happy with just having interesting Pandoran powers that a member of the Hundred Handed to learn. <br /> <br /> One of things I liked about the 1E Centimani was that they were written up as <b><i>seemingly</i></b> a completely legitimate philosophy and refinement. Utterly inhuman and monsterous but seemingly internally consistant, personalized and even progressive in some ways. Certainly the more scientific/rational aspects/examples from 1E massively struck a cord with me. As did the emotional underlying undertones of turning to Flux as a sort of refuge from the pain of failure and rejection. <br /> <br /> The reason I rate the Hundred Handed as the best protagonist/antagonist faction in 1E is that it took me a couple of readings to realise the level of self delusion and deception involved in their philosophy. Its like listening to the Joker talk in the Dark Knight about being an agent of Chaos and realizing its a purposeful deception rather then a genuine belief (to the point that some people still years later think he's telling the truth in that scene). It something that strikes you when you realize it and stays with you every time you rewatch the film/reread the book. I really liked that after the first reading on the 1E Centimani I was completely taken in by their pitch and only later realized the bullshit in there. It made me completely understand (on an intellectual level at least, I've never battled with depression so the emotional aspect is still a bit of an abstract for me) how a character could fall to become one of the Hundred Handed. <br /> <br /> Obviously this 2E write up goes in a little bit of a different direction out of the gate. Centimani are not longer a refinement. Their engagement is more with mosterousness and Chaos/entropy rather then straight out negativity and anti-humanity (though they seem to retain a large helping of the latter). The rational aspects of them have been toned back too, but I think that can still be emphasized on a personal level from character to character. I like the more obvious element of an entropic slide/degradation (I fear my 40K background is leaking through) away from the ideal of the New Dawn rather then a simple indulgence away from the Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> The key for me is to make the Centimani <i><b>seem</b></i> genuine, that they are a legitimate alternative path towards a set goal (the goal being become a monster) that go about their goal with the same level of dedication, philosophy and understanding as the <u>true</u> Refinements. That while they are a turning away from the path of the New Dawn, they have their own system of belief and experiences to draw upon towards their own person goal. <br /> <br /> Then I want that rug of seemingly legitimacy to be pulled out from under them. That their theories when taken to their logical end are recursive, that their so-called progress is degradation, that their &quot;evolution&quot; is a dead end. Its all a lie. A well constructed, very convincing, easily internalized falsehood or delusion that the hurt, tired and despairing Promethean can easily fall into precisely because it looks like its a legitimate path, that its o so convincing at face value and base assumption. <br /> <br /> If you can do that to the same extent with this 2E take on the Hundred Handed Eberg that the writers managed in 1E Promethean you will have me hook-line-an-sinker for this game. <br /> <br /> So you know...no pressure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T19:05:49-08:00","id":318635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=318382#post318382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The key for me is to make the Centimani <i><b>seem</b></i> genuine, that they are a legitimate alternative path towards a set goal (the goal being become a monster) that go about their goal with the same level of dedication, philosophy and understanding as the <u>true</u> Refinements. That while they are a turning away from the path of the New Dawn, they have their own system of belief and experiences to draw upon towards their own person goal.<br /> <br /> Then I want that rug of seemingly legitimacy to be pulled out from under them. That their theories when taken to their logical end are recursive, that their so-called progress is degradation, that their &quot;evolution&quot; is a dead end. Its all a lie. A well constructed, very convincing, easily internalized falsehood or delusion that the hurt, tired and despairing Promethean can easily fall into precisely because it looks like its a legitimate path, that its o so convincing at face value and base assumption.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In a more light hearted context.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/7a/d6/cf/7ad6cf6c46a455fd994fcb9f47e3779e.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T22:26:48-08:00","id":318721,"title":"","content":"I can't really give specifics without Matt's approval, but I think that folks will be pleased. The Refinement of Flux is written up just like the other Refinements, with ethos, practices, and philosophy, and I don't think I'll get in trouble confirming that it has its own Transmutation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T04:20:18-08:00","id":318848,"title":"","content":"As opposed to free access to Pandoran Transmutations? That <i>is</i> news. And surprising, as I\u2019d think that the most definitive distinction between \u201cRefinement\u201d and \u201cnot a Refinement\u201d would be access to Transmutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T20:11:05-08:00","id":319575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=318848#post318848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As opposed to free access to Pandoran Transmutations? That <i>is</i> news. And surprising, as I\u2019d think that the most definitive distinction between \u201cRefinement\u201d and \u201cnot a Refinement\u201d would be access to Transmutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. At this point, I'm really starting to wonder just what exactly a Refinement is. I figured that Transmutations were integral to the Pilgrimage, and Refinements were the best manner of learning them. Philosophical exercises to uncover properties of the Azoth, and all that. Not that Pandoran magics weren't black, but putting up a divide between them and what the Hundred-Handed learn suggests an odd dichotomy, the necessity of which I hope is someday explained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T20:51:55-08:00","id":319589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=319575#post319575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that Pandoran magics weren't black, but putting up a divide between them and what the Hundred-Handed learn suggests an odd dichotomy, the necessity of which I hope is someday explained.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly suspect that things like Zeus's Benediction, Mantle of Lordship, and the general weirdness of the Sublimati are a contributing factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T00:20:26-08:00","id":319694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=318848#post318848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As opposed to free access to Pandoran Transmutations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Refinement favors TWO Transmutation types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T16:36:54-08:00","id":320246,"title":"","content":"Yes; but the Centimani aren\u2019t a Refinement. And in 1e, they didn\u2019t get two Transmutation types; all they got was the ability to pick up Pandoran Transmutations without the risk of degeneration \u2014 one could even argue that that protection was supposed to be <i>in place of</i> the Affinity Transmutation price break; though I can easily see that argument going either way, and won\u2019t pursue that notion any further. <br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m not opposed to the notion of 2e\u2019s Centimani getting Transmutations of their own; I just wasn\u2019t taking it as a given that they <i>would</i> get anything beyond 2e\u2019s equivalent of Pandoran Transmutations (which, according to this, don\u2019t appear to be Transmutations at all), because they didn\u2019t in 1e and because it clashes a bit with the notion that they\u2019re not a Refinement. But if Centimani Transmutations do something that Dread Powers don\u2019t do and they help highlight the themes of the Centimani, then sure; more power to them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-23-2014, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T20:53:56-08:00","id":320339,"title":"","content":"Off-topic but I thought anyone who wasn't watching the blog would want a heads up.<br /> <br /> Basically it boils down to <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/than-longen-folk-to-goon-on-pilgrimages-promethean-the-created/\" target=\"_blank\">Milestones or Roles?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T12:54:54-08:00","id":323109,"title":"","content":"Well. That's ... boring. Honestly, if the game is actually like this (and it isn't just Matt's writeups) then I'll probably just port 1st ed. Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=317946#post317946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the writer of the Centimani section, I'd love to hear more feedback that isn't tied up in the whole transhumanism perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose I'm playing one of the many genderqueer sample characters. So I try and alter my (gendered) body to fit my self-image.<br /> <br /> Is this <i>counter to the Pilgrimage?</i> Will it inevitably lead me into madness and self-mutilation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=316627#post316627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanist game. &quot;But what if assholes&quot; is a shit response in that it gleefully kickflips past the themes and necessary buy-in and you're beginning to tax my already-not-stellar reserves of patience by doing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a World of Darkness game, mate. Assholes <i>exist</i>. If the themes are incompatible with that, the game is broken.<br /> <br /> I think it's more likely you're misinterpreting the themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-26-2014, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T14:20:10-08:00","id":323166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323109#post323109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. That's ... boring. Honestly, if the game is actually like this (and it isn't just Matt's writeups) then I'll probably just port 1st ed. Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could comment on the rest, but I think the heart of the problem is this:<br /> <br /> <i>1st Edition Promethean is about all of these things too. The games themes haven't changed at all</i>.<i>Your problems are ingrained in the very nature of the game.</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T14:32:48-08:00","id":323179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323109#post323109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Suppose I'm playing one of the many genderqueer sample characters. So I try and alter my (gendered) body to fit my self-image.<br /> <br /> Is this <i>counter to the Pilgrimage?</i> Will it inevitably lead me into madness and self-mutilation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait how did you get from a Promethean deciding its gender norms (which is a pretty damn human thing to do, and so would be part of the Pilgrimage) to becoming Centimani? Because I saw nothing in the Hundred Handed preview that even mildly suggested such a thing would be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T14:35:18-08:00","id":323180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323179#post323179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait how did you get from a Promethean deciding its gender norms (which is a pretty damn human thing to do, and so would be part of the Pilgrimage) to becoming Centimani? Because I saw nothing in the Hundred Handed preview that even mildly suggested such a thing would be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm know, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T16:44:47-08:00","id":323234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323109#post323109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. That's ... boring. Honestly, if the game is actually like this (and it isn't just Matt's writeups) then I'll probably just port 1st ed. Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>In an attempt to be less confrontational about it: what do you see in this writeup that strikes you as different from what 1e does (and thus is solvable by sticking with 1e)? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323109#post323109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suppose I'm playing one of the many genderqueer sample characters. So I try and alter my (gendered) body to fit my self-image.<br /> <br /> Is this <i>counter to the Pilgrimage?</i> Will it inevitably lead me into madness and self-mutilation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to my knowledge, no. <br /> <br /> I won\u2019t be surprised at any of the following existing in 2e:<br /> \u2022 Roles for one of the Refinements that represent exploring different notions of gender identity. <br /> \u2022 At least one Transmutation (<i>not</i> Pandoran and <i>not</i> Centimani) that allows the Promethean to alter his or her sex. This strikes me as far less radical than some of the physical alteration Transmutations that 1e already provides. <br /> \u2022 The ability to achieve the New Dawn as something other than strictly male or female, physically. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323109#post323109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a World of Darkness game, mate. Assholes <i>exist</i>. If the themes are incompatible with that, the game is broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assholes exist; but that doesn\u2019t mean that humans are assholes by default. <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s buy-in is that even though human assholes exist, humanity is still, on the whole, a worthwhile thing to want to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-27-2014, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T00:39:18-08:00","id":323488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323234#post323234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assholes exist; but that doesn\u2019t mean that humans are assholes by default. <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s buy-in is that even though human assholes exist, humanity is still, on the whole, a worthwhile thing to want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in the WoD, humans are social animals and even in the face of major disasters, tend to be focused on helping each other. Civilization is based on this principle and if we were all just a collection of assholes, we would've never created civilization to begin with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 11-27-2014, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T00:58:03-08:00","id":323491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323109#post323109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a World of Darkness game, mate. Assholes <i>exist</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And, shockingly, they do not compose the entirety of the human species and they share many of their identifying qualities with the selfish lying monsters that populate the Saturnine Night. Humanity is far from the most stalwart and practiced of role models for passionate shortsighted self-gratification, particularly not when dealing with spirits is the traditional role of an entire Lineage. The line draws on references to the Prometheus myth for a reason.<br /> <br /> &quot;'But what if assholes' isn't a bad response because assholes,&quot; as a response, is incoherent and sophomoric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the themes are incompatible with that, the game is broken.<br /> <br /> I think it's more likely you're misinterpreting the themes. </div> </div> </div>Read the books, I implore you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T02:24:16-08:00","id":323546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The ability to achieve the New Dawn as something other than strictly male or female, physically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be really cool. Ovbious route is intersexed but as there's actual magic here maybe an actual hermafrodite? I mean, there's few things that say alchemical perfect human as well as a true Rebis.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Could that count as transhuman for those interested in exploring those thems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-27-2014, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T04:25:25-08:00","id":323568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323234#post323234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In an attempt to be less confrontational about it: what do you see in this writeup that strikes you as different from what 1e does (and thus is solvable by sticking with 1e)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same &quot;Centimani used to be sympathetic/an actual philosophy&quot; that's already been said by everyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assholes exist; but that doesn\u2019t mean that humans are assholes by default. <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s buy-in is that even though human assholes exist, humanity is still, on the whole, a worthwhile thing to want to be. </div> </div> </div>Well, sure. The game is supposed to sell Humanity as something much better than being a monster. But saying &quot;humans being assholes is against the game's themes&quot; doesn't do that, because in actual play humans are going to be assholes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323179#post323179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait how did you get from a Promethean deciding its gender norms (which is a pretty damn human thing to do, and so would be part of the Pilgrimage) to becoming Centimani? Because I saw nothing in the Hundred Handed preview that even mildly suggested such a thing would be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not deciding their gender norms, actually changing their physical sex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323234#post323234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won\u2019t be surprised at any of the following existing in 2e:<br /> \u2022 Roles for one of the Refinements that represent exploring different notions of gender identity.<br /> \u2022 At least one Transmutation (<i>not</i> Pandoran and <i>not</i> Centimani) that allows the Promethean to alter his or her sex. This strikes me as far less radical than some of the physical alteration Transmutations that 1e already provides.<br /> \u2022 The ability to achieve the New Dawn as something other than strictly male or female, physically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be good. What Refinement would that fall under, though?<br /> <br /> It seems to me that nuPromethean is about going from a freak to a &quot;normal person&quot;; first you find a (stereotypical) role in society, like &quot;housewife&quot; or &quot;soldier&quot;, and then when you get good enough at it you actually turn into one. The <i>self-discovery</i> is gone; it's less a metaphor for adolescence, and more (literal!) LGTBQ people being forced to &quot;fit in&quot; by societal disapproval - I'm sorry, I mean nuDisquiet - while we cheer on the sidelines because that's The Way It's Supposed To Be.<br /> <br /> But, again, this is me <i>wildly</i> extrapolating from Matt's spoilers. It may well be - indeed, there's a pretty high chance that it <i>is</i> - a complete misinterpretation of the actual game, Chinese-whispers style.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-28-2014, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T06:32:06-08:00","id":323597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323568#post323568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sure. The game is supposed to sell Humanity as something much better than being a monster. Butsaying &quot;humans being assholes is against the game's themes&quot; doesn't do that, because in actual play humans are going to be assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are aware that &quot;humans being assholes is against the game's themes&quot; is not actually an interchangeable argument with &quot;saying 'but there are humans who are assholes!' is not an argument against humanity as a state of existence being a worthwhile pursuit,&quot; yes? Because I had kind of hoped &quot;people suck, let's whine about it&quot; was a sentiment we had all gotten over by late high school age. The things that set humanity apart from the rest of the World of Darkness are not &quot;they can be assholes just like everybody else.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems to me that nuPromethean is about going from a freak to a &quot;normal person&quot;; first you find a (stereotypical) role in society, like &quot;housewife&quot; or &quot;soldier&quot;, and then when you get good enough at it you actually turn into one. </div> </div> </div>Stereotypical roles in society that <i>you develop understandings of more than one of</i> as a means of constructing a multifaceted understanding of how humans are multiple things and that <i>are incredibly broadly manifested.</i> You're meant to go through these things as part of finalizing that last bulwark against being thought of as &quot;the thing that doesn't have a place here&quot; by getting enough fixed examples to set &quot;has a place&quot; as a constant quality instead of a rider on &quot;is a [human archetype represented by a Role].&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The <i>self-discovery</i> is gone; it's less a metaphor for adolescence, and more (literal!) LGTBQ people <b>being forced to &quot;fit in&quot; by societal disapproval - I'm sorry, I mean nuDisquiet - while we cheer on the sidelines because that's The Way It's Supposed To Be.</b> </div> </div> </div>1. Matt's <i>explicitly</i> said that the &quot;you're a thing that Should Not Be&quot; aspect of 1e is something he's seeking to de-emphasize in 2e.<br /> 2. Roles helping stop Disquiet if you master them causing a restrictive effect on one's presentation of what one is <i>if you </i><i><i>don't</i> move on to a new one</i> is <i>entirely contrary to &quot;the Pilgrimage makes you turn into a stereotype.&quot;</i><br /> 3. Another thing I had hoped we had all moved on from after high school: shitty &quot;[x] - [fake apology], I mean [y]&quot; sarcasm. If you're actually aiming to converse in good faith this is the complete opposite of a helpful tactic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, again, this is me <i>wildly</i> extrapolating from Matt's spoilers. It may well be - indeed, there's a pretty high chance that it <i>is</i> - a complete misinterpretation of the actual game, Chinese-whispers style. </div> </div> </div>Some of this isn't even as broad as &quot;wild extrapolation&quot; so much as it is &quot;wholesale invention of malicious misinformation based on near-maximally uncharitable readings.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-27-2014, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T08:11:38-08:00","id":323634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323568#post323568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The same &quot;Centimani used to be sympathetic/an actual philosophy&quot; that's already been said by everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm...the express point that I made (and a few other people talked about) in regards to the Centimani is that their FAKE appearance of being legitimate is what made them such interesting antagonist/protagonists. The fact that their philosophy was put across as one that might actually have something too it, but ultimately was a self-destructive and futile path made them feel very at home in both the WoD and Promethean.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear here the Centimani philosophy is not: <i><b>&quot;I'm going to be different from humanity as it is.&quot;</b></i><br /> The Centimani philosophy is: <i><b>&quot;I can never achieve humanity, its pointless. So I fall become a monster, something completely inhuman.&quot;</b></i><br /> <br /> Throw in all the stuff (that I've detailed before) about the nature of Flux (the driving force of the Centimani) its Alchemical representation (as dissolution without refinement) and its pretty obvious really that the Hundred Handed are going (namely no where good).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323568#post323568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not deciding their gender norms, actually changing their physical sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh OK in that case we need to get a bit more supernatural. However, off the top of my head there are at least 2 Transmutations which should let you do that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Obviously, your going to want to set that up a bit before trying to pull off a role as another sex. Likely get another set of fake documents made for the female/male you, introduce yourself to a new set of people who don't know the previous female/male version of you. Its likely to be something I can imagine a Promethean doing once they have moved to a new area and are taking on a new role.<br /> <br /> Entirely doable though and certainly and interesting thing to explore on ones Pilgrimage. I could see it falling under Aurum (seeing how human society treats females differently from males) or Plumbum (as its experimenting with your innate Promethean abilities and form). At a stretch you might also do that sorta thing in Cuprum (to see a different point of view via different &quot;observation affect&quot; of your form) or Argentum (if you were studying/blending in with a group of Supernaturals who can and do change their forms often).<br /> <br /> Nothing involved in the exploration of the different physical sexes (or even some non-binary combination) is inherently of the Hundred Handed. The only sort of thing in regards to genre and sex which might fall under the Centimani would be not wanting to be any gender or sex that the human body could support. I guess they stuff like your sterotypical horrific inuman hentai-like tentacle monster or parasitic style reproductive stuff like the Alien/Xenomorph life cycle (implanting people with bits of their flesh that grow tumour like into servitors for them &quot;their children&quot;) would fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T10:18:38-08:00","id":323732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323568#post323568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, again, this is me <i>wildly</i> extrapolating from Matt's spoilers. It may well be - indeed, there's a pretty high chance that it <i>is</i> - a complete misinterpretation of the actual game, Chinese-whispers style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you extrapolating, particularly <i>that</i> wildly and <i>that </i>broadly (and <i>that </i>negatively)? The text is pretty clear on it's own.<br /> <br /> You <i>do</i> remember Matt basically masterminded all of the Promethean supplements, right?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, how is this like Chinese whispers in any way, shape, or form? We're dealing with first-hand sources here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-27-2014, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T11:10:07-08:00","id":323773,"title":"","content":"Also, you seem to be fixating a bit too much on the \u201callegory for LGBTQ issues\u201d thing. <b>Promethean</b> isn\u2019t a game about social outcasts learning to accept that there\u2019s nothing wrong with them; it\u2019s a game about subhuman beings learning how to become human. This isn\u2019t new to the second edition; it has always been true of <b>Promethean</b>. So <i>of course</i> a simple overlay of LGBTQ issues is going to come across as offensive. That\u2019s not a condemnation of the game, though; if anything, it\u2019s the fault of the player for attempting such a simplistic approach to what is a rather complex situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T11:32:06-08:00","id":323779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323568#post323568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that nuPromethean is about going from a freak to a &quot;normal person&quot;; first you find a (stereotypical) role in society, like &quot;housewife&quot; or &quot;soldier&quot;, and then when you get good enough at it you actually turn into one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a ridiculously inaccurate read of Roles. Turning into one is <i>bad</i>: that's what risks a Blighted Wasteland. That's what the whole Stuck in a Rut section is about. Turning into a stereotype is a massive mistake because you've turned <i>away</i> from self-discovery.<br /> <br /> The point of Roles is to experiment with stereotypes in order to understand them. <i>Then you move on</i>. You try out housewife for a while and say, &quot;But I don't like being a housewife,&quot; and you move on. Or you say, &quot;I like the sense of family, but I don't like staying at home all the time.&quot; You've discovered something about yourself and achieved a Milestone. Look at the Milestones for Companion. You can sufficiently understand being a Companion by <i>getting shunned</i>.<br /> <br /> And it really says something that you've managed to have this discussion in the wrong thread. Something about reading comprehension, mainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T11:37:22-08:00","id":323784,"title":"","content":"The point to Roles is not to just act out the form, but to understand the what's and why's behind it-the heart of why people become soldiers or caretakers or killers or assholes. Society has a place for drones, which is why Prommies just drudging the role can mitigate their Disquiet, but a Prommie-hell, a person who wants to really find their identity needs to ask how and why and particular form of thing they'll be. Add in the complex layers of personal interpretations of archetypes, and it's easy to see how a Prommie can use that to move them along the Pilgramage.<br /> <br /> You like sushi, but <i>why</i> do you like sushi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T20:32:40-08:00","id":324171,"title":"","content":"And as mentioned, the metaphor isn't &quot;Outsider changing himself to be accepted&quot;, it's &quot;feral child learning to understand the world she was never a part of&quot;. It's growing up, when you have little idea how.<br /> <br /> Disquiet isn't social disapproval at all, it's tension produced by humans subconsciously realizing they're standing to unshielded Azothic radiation, combined with growing sick from that same radiation (the sickness is of the mind, but still).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T21:43:34-08:00","id":324205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=324171#post324171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as mentioned, the metaphor isn't &quot;Outsider changing himself to be accepted&quot;, it's &quot;feral child learning to understand the world she was never a part of&quot;. It's growing up, when you have little idea how.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the minor thematics of &quot;this is how hard it is to make a genuinely new person and have it stick&quot; at work in the Pilgrimage, it's worth pointing out that any reading of the material that assumes Mortality is subsumption rather than integration is objectively a poor one. You may just forget your Created experiences when you finally grasp the Aurora, but the soul is not the ego or the conscious memory and the New Dawn adds another patch to the vast quilt of humanity regardless of how you're Redeemed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T07:03:12-08:00","id":324472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323597#post323597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I had kind of hoped &quot;people suck, let's whine about it&quot; was a sentiment we had all gotten over by late high school age. The things that set humanity apart from the rest of the World of Darkness are not &quot;they can be assholes just like everybody else.&quot;<br /> [...]<br /> Another thing I had hoped we had all moved on from after high school: shitty &quot;[x] - [fake apology], I mean [y]&quot; sarcasm. If you're actually aiming to converse in good faith this is the complete opposite of a helpful tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't ... <i>think</i> I said that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323597#post323597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stereotypical roles in society that <i>you develop understandings of more than one of</i> as a means of constructing a multifaceted understanding of how humans are multiple things and that <i>are incredibly broadly manifested.</i> You're meant to go through these things as part of finalizing that last bulwark against being thought of as &quot;the thing that doesn't have a place here&quot; by getting enough fixed examples to set &quot;has a place&quot; as a constant quality instead of a rider on &quot;is a [human archetype represented by a Role].&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, good point.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323732#post323732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you extrapolating, particularly <i>that</i> wildly and <i>that </i>broadly (and <i>that </i>negatively)? The text is pretty clear on it's own.<br /> [...]<br /> <br /> Also, how is this like Chinese whispers in any way, shape, or form? We're dealing with first-hand sources here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm dealing with my interpretation of the implications of Matt's description of the writer's attempt to convey an idea.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=323634#post323634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ummm...the express point that I made (and a few other people talked about) in regards to the Centimani is that their FAKE appearance of being legitimate is what made them such interesting antagonist/protagonists. The fact that their philosophy was put across as one that might actually have something too it, but ultimately was a self-destructive and futile path made them feel very at home in both the WoD and Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. &quot;X gives you power but makes you evil&quot; is much less interesting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=324171#post324171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as mentioned, the metaphor isn't &quot;Outsider changing himself to be accepted&quot;, it's &quot;feral child learning to understand the world she was never a part of&quot;. It's growing up, when you have little idea how.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T12:11:45-08:00","id":324717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=324472#post324472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Right. &quot;X gives you power but makes you evil&quot; is much less interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes it would be.<br /> <br /> However, no version of Promethean (1E or 2E) has represented the Centimani like that.<br /> <br /> Really the only differences between 1E Hundred Handed and 2E Hundred Handed are:<br /> <br /> 1) More of a focus on Choas and Entropy in 2E over self-styling yourself a monster (though the latter is still present).<br /> <br /> 2) The focus on a more instinctual and emotional aspect to the Centimani process in 2E. Though the &quot;cold alien thought forms&quot; of the 1E also still exist as one of the examples provided, its just less the norm.<br /> <br /> 3) The Hundred Handed are not recognized as a Refinement. Mainly because what refinements are, namely learning about being human, has nothing to do with being a member of the Hundred Handed.<br /> <br /> 4) They have their own unique set of Transmutations as opposed to &quot;just&quot; getting Pandoran transmutations. <br /> <br /> That's it, otherwise they are (as far as we can tell from the preview) the same group they were in 1E. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T18:58:42-08:00","id":324946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=324472#post324472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't ... <i>think</i> I said that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious as to why you lumped my second reference to petty high school misanthropy into the quote you attached this to, given that &quot;[x], [apology that is either fake or a demonstration of a bizarre inability to comprehend the function of the delete key in relation to realizing one has made an error in the middle of typing a post], I mean [y]&quot; is <i>exactly what that line was a response to.</i><br /> <br /> As for the first, let's unpack this:<br /> \u2022 Metamurpho makes a claim of black-and-white morality at work (we shall, for expediency's sake, not dwell on the matter of how Flux has always unambiguously been a bad thing outside the context of 'murph's headcanons), citing humanity's capacity for evil as a mark against the Pilgrimage being unambiguously a good thing (for which see my earlier note of &quot;this much raw world-shifting energy does not have a positive effect on anything unless channeled into a more refined output&quot;).<br /> \u2022 I point out that a humanist game - i.e. a game whose themes include the notion that being human is a worthwhile state of existence - does not benefit from humoring an appeal to the potential morality of human beings as an excuse for giving more positive pagespace to attempts to complete one's transformation as something other than human, particularly in a game whose core narrative is &quot;an inhuman being attempts to learn enough about humanity to develop more than an imitation of it.&quot;<br /> \u2022 You somehow interpret this as &quot;humanism as a philosophy and a set of themes is incompatible with humanity being capable of evil or obnoxiousness.&quot; You also decide, completely arbitrarily, that <i>I'm</i> the one misinterpreting the themes of the game.<br /> \u2022 I point out that 1) humanity being capable of those things does not render them incapable of anything else, least of all their notional opposites and 2) there are many beings in the World of Darkness - including the failed siblings of the Prometheans and the beings the Ulgans occasionally truck with - who are capable of the aforementioned things but largely incapable of the aforementioned opposite things. (Remember how Pandoran Willpower recovery works in 1e. Remember also how ghosts and spirits recover Willpower in 2e and what this implies about their priorities.)<br /> \u2022 You take nothing from any of this, instead going on to repeat your initial error in response to Hawthorn, seemingly referring back to my response to Metamurpho.<br /> \u2022 I make the &quot;assholes existing among humanity does not contradict humanity being a worthwhile state&quot; thing more explicit and note my general disappointment with arguments that sound like a baby nihilist came up with them.<br /> \u2022 You are confused by this, and here we are today.<br /> <br /> Spirits are noted to be essentially &quot;programmed&quot; creatures, incapable of seeing the world through lenses not colored by their purviews and their self-centered myopia; incapable of genuine charity, faith, hope, empathy, or creativity; they can be remarkably complex in their makeup and a hidden exception could exist for almost any directive that comprises their thought processes, but by and large the ability to do things without expecting compensation, entertain a thought without believing it, believe in something without evidence, and other such sublime irrationality is the province of humanity and its ontological immediate family. Most everything else runs on sufficiently advanced arrangements of conditionals and paths the monsters follow.<br /> <br /> To err is human.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Salient fantasy novel quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hand of Oberon, Chapter 4, Dworkin Barimen, </strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;You still do not understand,&quot; he said. &quot;I cannot but think that a damaged thing should be destroyed - and hopefully replaced. The nature of my personal injury is such that I cannot envision repair. I am damaged in just this fashion. My feelings are foreordained.&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-29-2014, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T21:00:42-08:00","id":325035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=324472#post324472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm dealing with my interpretation of the implications of Matt's description of the writer's attempt to convey an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mug, you asked a question with the point of accusation about if LBGQT was a Centimani thing after Matt flatly said that he is motivated by a sense of inviting everyone to the table that explicitly mentions this sort of stuff.<br /> <br /> There's interpretation, and then there's people making stuff up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T12:14:23-08:00","id":325472,"title":"","content":"Jeez, everybody take a breath. <br /> <br /> OK, so, MugaSofer actually brought something up that I find interesting from &quot;game design meets actually gaming&quot; standpoint, and that is: If a Promethean wants to alter hir body to the point of changing biological sex (never mind gender identity/presentation, which is a different thing), does that propel the Promethean in the direction of Centimani? <br /> <br /> Absent any other data, I would say no. Gender conflict is a very real part of being human, it's just something that a good number of us don't have to deal with on a regular basis. So I would say that <i>depending on how the player wants to approach it</i>, taking into account he character's Pilgrimage thus far and the overall context of the game, I'd be more likely to see that character heading for Cuprum (which has a Transmutation based around physically changing the body), Aurum (all things humanity, sex and gender included), or Cobalus (humanity, some cultures more than others, have some really weird hangups about gender and sex and identity, and figuring out where those transgression points lie would be very much in keeping for Cobalt).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T14:52:10-08:00","id":325577,"title":"","content":"Matt, as a person who's not played a huge amount of Promethean, forgive my ignorance - do Centimani tend to be loners or do you get Throngs of them like Pilgrims?<br /> <br /> Also: is Pilgrim a pertinent term when referring to Prometheans who are seeking to become human, because it seems appropriate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T17:22:38-08:00","id":325662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=325577#post325577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt, as a person who's not played a huge amount of Promethean, forgive my ignorance - do Centimani tend to be loners or do you get Throngs of them like Pilgrims?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking from a 1e perspective, at least: While obviously it varies from setting to setting and table to table, the low numbers of the Created and the lower-still numbers of the Hundred-Handed tends to mean that the bulk of those a throng will encounter will be solitary. Groups like the Epimetheans or the Created portion of the Cult of Chains tend to be rarer but commensurately more troublesome.<br /> <br /> That said, the Extempore writeup from Magnum Opus makes mention of the possibility of throngs of serendipitously-Created Freaks, which I've thought was a neat little storyhook with potential for evocative imagery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T21:17:43-08:00","id":325775,"title":"","content":"Also, centimani tend to be pandoran tamers too, so even those without a throng are probably beast masters instead of lone wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T08:18:29-08:00","id":326019,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just logistically you figure they'd be loners.<br /> <br /> That said, what if a throng decided, collectively, to say &quot;screw the Pilgrimage&quot; and all become Freaks? Gah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T12:02:21-08:00","id":327273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=326019#post326019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, just logistically you figure they'd be loners.<br /> <br /> That said, what if a throng decided, collectively, to say &quot;screw the Pilgrimage&quot; and all become Freaks? Gah.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sing-song to the tune of the alligator scene in All Dogs Go to Heaven*<br /> Let's make monsters together!<br /> Let's make disharmony!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T20:52:37-08:00","id":344342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev?p=326019#post326019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, just logistically you figure they'd be loners.<br /> <br /> That said, what if a throng decided, collectively, to say &quot;screw the Pilgrimage&quot; and all become Freaks? Gah.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here I was hoping to be original! Dammit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}